      "message": "nit: I think this is more readable by inverting the branches, and using early out:\n\n```\n                if (auto result \u003d fuzzer.fn(mod, data); result !\u003d Success) {\n                    if (options.verbose) {\n                        std::cout \u003c\u003c \"   Failed to execute fuzzer: \" \u003c\u003c result.Failure() \u003c\u003c \"\\n\";\n                    }\n                    return;\n                }\n                if (tint::core::ir::Validate(mod, fuzzer.post_capabilities) !\u003d Success) {\n                    TINT_ICE()\n                        \u003c\u003c \"Failed to validate against fuzzer capabilities after running, \"\n                        \u003c\u003c currently_running \u003c\u003c \"\\n\";\n                }\n```\n\nSame for the code below.",
